{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["The sense of <b>and the Mizpah</b>: Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 31:49): 'and the Mizpah which is in the hill country of Gilead,' as it is written (Judges 11:29) 'and he passed through Mizpeh Gilead.' Why was it called Mizpah? Because each one of them said to the other, 'May HaShem watch (יצף).' If so, it is the name of a high place at the top of the mountain. In my opinion, it is the stone that Jacob set up as a pillar, and he drew from this the name, calling it Gale'ed; and he called it Mizpah because he said, 'May HaShem watch (יצף).' And it is possible that it is 'Mizpeh Gilead' (see Judges 11:29), that the place was called after the name of this stone forever."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:09.219208877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}